From 9a3560c1f41db5af60d64e4bc14650574ac2ebed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:26:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] net: macb: add MStar/SigmaStar EMAC support

The MStar/SigmaStar EMAC is an AT91RM9200 style MACB behind the RIU,
where every 32-bit register is split over two 16-bit slots.

- RIU register accessors (MACB_CAPS_MSTAR_RIU)
- the at91ether transmit path generalised to a ring of 2 (RM9200) or
  4 (MStar, MACB_CAPS_MSTAR_TXQ, free count read from TSR) entries,
  reset on every open
- msc313_init(): quiesce whatever the previous owner left running,
  switch to software RX descriptors, external PHY magic
- never printk while holding bp->lock in start_xmit: with netconsole
  on the same interface the message re-enters through netpoll

Based on the linux-chenxing macb changes (Daniel Palmer), rewritten
on top of 7.3 with new capability bits (the chenxing ones collided with
MIIONRGMII/NEED_TSUCLK) and corrected ring index arithmetic.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
